    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a10">

                <pb facs="0700" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg610"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in 4 in No. 731.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Badeau to General Schenck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1875-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 15, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the previous correspondence on
                    the subject of the attempted transfer of nationality of the American vessel “G.
                    C. Trufant,” I have the honor now to forward a communication from the American
                    consul at Liverpool, of the 13th instant, on the same subject, establishing the
                    fact, by his own admission, that the owner of the vessel is a British
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>ADAM BADEAU,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">General Schenck</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
